{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"MERGED as commit 1e7e5c946 (Gerrit change 970), LLM-Review +1 / Verified +1, landed after its dependency 72d9 (change 968) per the recorded order-of-work. Every AC met: (1) a source=local PASS returns signature.signed=False with the machine-readable reason local-source-never-signs (test_local_source_pass_is_never_signed); (2) after a local PASS, claim_gate_check reports ok=False and rebar claim is blocked with the ticket still open (test_local_source_review_leaves_the_claim_gate_blocked); (3) test_pass_verdict_carries_a_passing_signature now reviews attested — the bypass is no longer encoded as expected behavior; (4) never-sign coverage spans BLOCK/INDETERMINATE/degraded/local/sign=False; (5) the no-null-verified_at_sha invariant is enforced at the single signing seam (sign_plan_review + refresh_attestation, which now also binds the pin it previously omitted) and asserted by test_no_signed_attestation_can_carry_a_null_verified_at_sha; the recovery path signs inside an attested fetch=False gate session and refuses local-source sidecars (sidecar now records source; test_sign_review_refuses_to_resign_a_local_source_pass + test_sign_review_recovery_binds_a_committed_verified_at_sha + test_drift_refreshed_attestation_carries_a_verified_at_sha); (6) docs/plan-review-gate.md states the never-signs rule and the offline attested recipe; (7) gates green. Store audit (earlier comment): 0 of 69 existing attestations carried a null pin — no retroactive invalidation needed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785008141637998001,"uuid":"b76216e4-64fb-4d66-8c45-1e6b6f0901bc"}